    "id": "triton-flow",
    "caption": "Triton puts a scheduler and dynamic batcher in front of every model, so concurrent requests are grouped into batches and run on whichever backend the model's config names.",
    "alt": "Clients send requests over HTTP on port 8000 or gRPC on port 8001 using the KServe v2 protocol. Triton routes each request to the model's scheduler, where the dynamic batcher groups concurrent requests. Batches run on model instances: an ONNX Runtime instance group on the GPU, a Python backend for pre- and post-processing, and a vLLM backend for an LLM.",
